The design to build against, for your review before any code (docs/inputs.md):
- the three kinds of input: request–fulfil (the app's to-do lists), declare, and source declarations (where to fetch from, in a standard format);
- the drop boxes' layout on the NAS;
- per input: its shape (exact fields, types, an example), its checks (errors and warnings), how ingesting and rebuilding follow, and how today's data moves into the shape;
- the inventory: every place the app's code names a specific source (URLs, hand lists, a function per register, per-dataset code, credits), each marked as becoming a declaration field, moving out to a producer, or staying as generic code.

The decisions from our discussion (9 Oct) are the requirements: regions as files with GeoJSON for custom shapes; one timetable input worldwide (declared GTFS feeds, plus static GTFS you compile by hand, no expiry, frequencies.txt allowed); heritage as one GeoJSON per register (any geometry) plus a description file, located before it's dropped, matching by rule in the build and your same/not-same pairs as an input; elevation as a description per dataset (GeoTIFF files or URLs, or a tile pyramid in a declared encoding; ground or surface; height reference; licence), any resolution, ranked and blended; languages by territory as a declare input.
